## Summary

This PR executes the bounded image-first external-VLM lane authorized by #1612 and preserves its fail-closed terminal outcome.

It freezes the exact current `origin/main`, four complete Spring 2022 official 9709 papers, the exact 12-question diagnostic inherited from merged #1577, deterministic render/crop parameters, the minimal visual-truth schema, the current provider/model/endpoint and native-CNY price snapshot, immutable run/checkpoint paths, review-time threshold, and role isolation. Official image bytes and raw candidate responses remain in the repo-external immutable evidence root; the repository contains their hashes, source bindings, cost receipts, matrices, validators, and report.

A separate read-only checker committed official-page observations before producer reveal. It accepted 34/34 source objects and verified 167/167 bound files with zero hash mismatch or blocker.

## Execution result

C0 ran exactly 12/12 authorized diagnostic questions with:

- CNY 0.071160 cumulative provider cost;
- 100% usage, response-ID, request-hash, response-hash, and image-hash coverage;
- zero question identity, page-chain, visible-subpart, visible-mark, or required-visual loss;
- zero next-question/tail-page contamination in the formal fields;
- zero unauthorized payloads, remote data-service writes, sealed/old-Gold/candidate-answer access, or production/public display.

The frozen validator then found the same candidate-enhancement schema defect in all 12 responses: `reading_order_notes` and `semantic_notes` were strings instead of arrays. That produced a 100% protocol/schema failure rate and repeated the same critical defect, triggering the issue's mandatory wave stop. C1 and C2 were not called, no schema was loosened, and no immutable response was rewritten or normalized after observation.

The terminal verdict is `ITERATE_WITH_SMALLER_TRUTH`. No formal object is promoted and no GO, product-readiness, display-rights, or canonical-truth claim is made.

