## What changed

This repair replaces the absolute `x < 65` MS question-digit heuristic with a source-grounded locator that:

- normalizes PDF words into rendered page coordinates, including the rotated 2017 layouts;
- binds explicit layouts to the official `Question` / `Answer` / `Marks` table topology;
- resolves older borderless layouts only when one complete ordered question column is uniquely supported by mark-code rows;
- rejects missing, reordered, duplicate-root, competing/formula, and invalid-region candidates fail closed;
- builds bounded MS region chains in the same normalized coordinate space and caches per-paper headers during packet preparation.

The user-visible effect is that genuine 2017 question rows are no longer rejected before checker dispatch, while formula digits, furniture, totals, gaps, and ambiguous sequences remain ineligible.

## Evidence and preservation

